   "id": "math.solve-fractions",
   "name": "Clearing fractions with the LCM",
   "requires": [
    "math.lcm"
   ],
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "To solve an equation with fractions, multiply both sides by the LCM of the denominators. The fractions disappear. Then solve as before. For x/3 + 5 = 7, multiply by 3: x + 15 = 21, so x = 6."
    }
   },
   "screens": [
    {
     "kind": "guess",
     "step": "hook",
     "title": "Clear the fraction",
     "ask": "x/3 + 5 = 7. Which number can you multiply both sides by to remove the fraction?",
     "opts": [
      "3",
      "5",
      "7",
      "15"
     ],
     "after": "Multiplying by 3 turns x/3 into x: x + 15 = 21, so x = 6.",
     "ref": "Activity 3.2.3 Q2 c",
     "id": "g7.maths.u3.s3-2-2.1"
    },
    {
     "kind": "read",
     "step": "read",
     "title": "Note",
     "paras": [
      "To solve linear equations involving fractions:",
      "Step 1. Find the least common multiple (LCM) of the denominators.",
      "Step 2. Multiply both sides of the equation by the LCM.",
      "Step 3. Solve: variable terms to one side, constants to the other."
     ],
     "id": "g7.maths.u3.s3-2-2.2"
    },
    {
     "kind": "steps",
     "step": "method",
     "title": "Solve (x + 2)/4 = 5/3",
     "steps": [
      "(x + 2)/4 = 5/3",
      "The LCM of 4 and 3 is 12. Multiply both sides by 12.",
      "12 ÷ 4 = 3 and 12 ÷ 3 = 4, so 3(x + 2) = 4(5).",
      "Remove the bracket: 3x + 6 = 20.",
      "3x = 20 − 6 = 14.",
      "Divide by 3: x = 14/3 = 4 2/3."
     ],
     "ref": "Example 8 a",
     "needs": "math.lcm",
     "id": "g7.maths.u3.s3-2-2.3"
    },
    {
     "kind": "steps",
     "step": "method",
     "title": "Solve x/8 + 7/4 = 5/6",
     "steps": [
      "x/8 + 7/4 = 5/6",
      "The LCM of 8, 4 and 6 is 24. Multiply every term by 24.",
      "24 ÷ 8 = 3, 24 ÷ 4 = 6, 24 ÷ 6 = 4. So 3x + 6 × 7 = 4 × 5.",
      "3x + 42 = 20.",
      "3x = 20 − 42 = −22.",
      "x = −22/3 = −7 1/3."
     ],
     "ref": "Example 8 b",
     "id": "g7.maths.u3.s3-2-2.4"
    },
